        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-23T17:14:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this data structure be synchronized?",
      "revId": "77ada49d3522001b73791e7133ffeeb494f27459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5d4c959_ac81c8c1",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 405,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-05T20:55:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Possibly.  I feel like I reasoned myself into thinking that the DPM flag would essentially be serving as an indicator for when the reply is read-safe.  But I could be reasoned into something more precise.",
      "parentUuid": "70c878da_773cbcd5",
      "revId": "77ada49d3522001b73791e7133ffeeb494f27459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "806ac62f_416070c4",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 422,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-23T17:14:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you think of a reason that the EC would want to tell the AP about an unsolicited VDM response?",
      "revId": "77ada49d3522001b73791e7133ffeeb494f27459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "16ae3f76_ae6cfbe3",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 422,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-05T20:55:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mayhaps.  A random unsolicited VDM response feels like it would be a pretty basic protocol error on the one hand (firmware domain issue), but on the other it could have resulted from something the AP did with this API (ex. those port partners we\u0027ve seen that take 1 second to reply to DiscoverIdentity sometimes). \n\nSo I suppose I could be convinced either way. I\u0027ll cc Prashant for his AP API opinions.",
      "parentUuid": "806ac62f_416070c4",
      "revId": "77ada49d3522001b73791e7133ffeeb494f27459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4eb0beb3_454fe824",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 422,
      "author": {
        "id": 1181774
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-05T21:03:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So I suppose I could be convinced either way. I\u0027ll cc Prashant for his AP API opinions.\n\nI\u0027d move towards keeping the API as flexible as possible (without making it unwieldy). So, that means sending the VDM response up to the AP and letting it figure out what to do with it (it can drop it if necessary); of course, will defer to the EC experts regarding code complexity/maintenance burden in making that possible.\n\nHow often do we expect unsolicited VDM responses?",
      "parentUuid": "16ae3f76_ae6cfbe3",
      "revId": "77ada49d3522001b73791e7133ffeeb494f27459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9a0ad66_e1f8dd54",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 422,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-05T21:13:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Spec-wise, we should never expect an unsolicited response.  Practically speaking, we get some occasionally on a weird partner.  Usually the times where we\u0027ve seen what look like unsolicited ACKs they\u0027re actually weirdly delayed replies to something we sent 100\u0027s of ms earlier.  I can\u0027t recall any others off the top of my head",
      "parentUuid": "4eb0beb3_454fe824",
      "revId": "77ada49d3522001b73791e7133ffeeb494f27459",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
